{"name":"Overtake","hex":"#33557f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"overtake","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To pass a slower moving object or entity (on the side closest to oncoming traffic).","To become greater than something else in quantity, worth, etc."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of overtaking; an overtaking maneuver."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overtake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Overtake (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Overtake (オーバーテイク) is a 1992 Formula One racing video game based on the 1992 season produced by ZOOM Inc. for the X68000 and licensed by FOCA to Fuji Television."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8c/Overtake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Overtake_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q7113995"},{"title":"Overtaking","blocks":[{"text":"Overtaking or passing is the act of one vehicle going past another slower moving vehicle, travelling in the same direction, on a road. The lane used for overtaking another vehicle is often a passing lane farther from the road shoulder, which is to the left in places that drive on the right and to the right in places that drive on the left."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Prehitevanje.jpg/330px-Prehitevanje.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Overtaking","wikidata":"Q1931051"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Inhalen.gif/60px-Inhalen.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c7/Inhalen.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Inhalen.gif/60px-Inhalen.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&